{
  "capitulo": 7,
  "titulo_es": "Cuando tenga tiempo",
  "titulo": { "en": "When I have time" },
  "intro": { "en": "Cuando plus the subjunctive looks forward. Cuando plus the indicative is a habit." },
  "palabras": {
    "cuando": { "en": "when", "pron": "KWAN-do", "cat": "conjunction" },
    "tenga": { "en": "I/he/she has (subjunctive)", "pron": "TEN-ga", "cat": "verb" },
    "tengo": { "en": "I have", "pron": "TEN-go", "cat": "verb" },
    "llamaré": { "en": "I will call", "pron": "ya-ma-RE", "cat": "verb" },
    "leo": { "en": "I read", "pron": "LE-o", "cat": "verb" },
    "en cuanto": { "en": "as soon as", "pron": "en KWAN-to", "cat": "conjunction" },
    "llegue": { "en": "I/he/she arrives (subjunctive)", "pron": "YE-he", "cat": "verb", "consejo": "Before e, g sounds like j." },
    "tiempo": { "en": "time", "pron": "TYEM-po", "genero": "m" }
  },
  "bloques": [
    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": "Habit, or not yet",
      "texto": "A habit that already happens uses the ordinary present.\n\n- **Cuando tengo** tiempo, leo.\n\nSomething that has **not happened yet** uses the subjunctive.\n\n- **Cuando tenga** tiempo, te llamaré.\n- **En cuanto llegue**, te escribo.\n\nThe future idea can sit in the other half of the sentence (llamaré) or just in the meaning."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "dialogo",
      "titulo": "Later",
      "frases": [
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "Cuando tengo tiempo, leo.",
          "en": "When I have time, I read.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Cuando tengo tiempo", "habit"],
            ["leo", "I read"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Pablo",
          "es": "Cuando tenga tiempo, te llamaré.",
          "en": "When I have time, I'll call you.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Cuando tenga tiempo", "future when"],
            ["te llamaré", "I will call you"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "En cuanto llegue, te escribo.",
          "en": "As soon as I arrive, I'll write to you.",
          "analisis": [
            ["En cuanto llegue", "as soon as I arrive"],
            ["te escribo", "I write to you"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Pablo",
          "es": "Llámame cuando llegues.",
          "en": "Call me when you arrive.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Llámame", "call me"],
            ["cuando llegues", "when you arrive"]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "vocabulario",
      "palabras": ["cuando", "tenga", "tengo", "llamaré", "leo", "en cuanto", "llegue", "tiempo"]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "test",
      "id": "b1-cuando-futuro",
      "pregunta": { "en": "The call has not happened yet. Which one?" },
      "opciones": {
        "Cuando tenga tiempo, te llamaré": { "en": "Not yet: subjunctive in the cuando clause." },
        "Cuando tengo tiempo, leo": { "en": "That is a habit. It already happens." },
        "Ayer te llamé": { "en": "That is finished. It is the indefinido." }
      },
      "correcta": "Cuando tenga tiempo, te llamaré"
    },
    {
      "tipo": "huecos",
      "id": "b1-cuando-tenga",
      "pregunta": { "en": "Complete the future plan." },
      "frase": "Cuando ___ tiempo, te llamaré.",
      "audio": true,
      "opciones": {
        "tenga": { "en": "The time is still in the future, so the subjunctive." },
        "tengo": { "en": "Tengo would describe a habit." },
        "tuve": { "en": "Tuve is the past." }
      },
      "correcta": "tenga"
    }
  ]
}
